			"Message": "feat(Initialize): Implement ConfigureLog module for structured logging setup\n\nIntroduces the ConfigureLog module to centralize the initialization of the logging subsystem for the Air daemon. This module acts as the bridge between environment variables and the underlying `AirLibrary::Logging` infrastructure, ensuring that logs are captured from the very start of the application lifecycle.\n\nKey implementations:\n- **Environment Parsing**: Reads and validates `AIR_LOG_JSON` to toggle JSON formatted output and `AIR_LOG_FILE` to enable file-based logging.\n- **Security & Validation**: Performs checks on log file paths to ensure the target directory exists and is writable, preventing silent failures and potential path traversal issues.\n- **Format Support**: Facilitates switching between standard text and JSON formatted logs, catering to both development debugging and production aggregation.\n- **Error Resilience**: Implements a fallback strategy to `eprintln!` on stderr if the structured logger fails to initialize, ensuring critical startup errors are still visible.\n- **Unit Tests**: Includes tests verifying default configuration and graceful handling of invalid environment variable values.\n\nThis module completes the logging configuration layer required for observability within the Initialize component.",
			"SHA": "b325d0b981634eee5d793245a78177cbd54f3fef"
		},
