				73,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Initialize): Implement ValidateCommand module for CLI input sanitization\n\nIntroduces the ValidateCommand module to centralize input validation for the Air CLI. This ensures that command parameters adhere to strict security and formatting rules before any execution or network operations occur.\n\nKey implementations:\n- **Parameter Checks**: Validates string lengths for service names (1-64), configuration keys (1-256), and log filters (1-512).\n- **Range Validation**: Enforces numeric limits, such as restricting log tail counts to 1-10,000 lines.\n- **Security Hardening**: Detects potentially malicious input patterns and enforces length limits to prevent DoS attacks.\n- **User Feedback**: Returns specific error messages indicating why validation failed (e.g., \"Command name too long\").\n- **Unit Tests**: Includes test coverage for valid inputs and boundary violation scenarios.\n\nThis module fulfills the validation requirement defined in the Command module hierarchy, protecting the HandleCommand execution flow.",
			"SHA": "048090691c4fa7cfbd4ead6d9737d76f408f554a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-02T02:31:28Z",
