				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Initialize): Define Command module hierarchy\n\nEstablishes the module structure for the `Command` component by introducing `mod.rs`. This change encapsulates the CLI parsing and handling logic within a dedicated namespace, aligning with the project's architectural organization and ensuring the module is correctly recognized by the Rust compiler.\n\nKey changes:\n- Created `Source/Initialize/Command/mod.rs`.\n- Declared `ParseArguments`, `HandleCommand`, `ValidateCommand`, and `Connect` as public submodules.\n- Added convenience re-exports of key structs and functions to simplify external usage.",
			"SHA": "c08645392aae12157467e1d4070554126daaaffb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-02T02:30:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				70,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Initialize): Implement HandleCommand module for CLI dispatch and daemon interaction\n\nIntroduces the HandleCommand module to serve as the central execution engine for Air CLI commands. This layer bridges the CLI interface with the backend daemon, handling local commands and routing remote commands to the appropriate services.\n\nKey implementations:\n- **Main Dispatcher**: The HandleCommand function validates inputs using ValidateCommand and matches commands to their respective handlers (Help, Version, Status, Restart, Config, Metrics, Logs, Debug).\n- **Sub-Handlers**: Implemented distinct async handlers for ConfigCommand (Get, Set, Reload, Show, Validate) and DebugCommand (DumpState, DumpConnections, HealthCheck, Diagnostics).\n- **Daemon Interaction**: Integrated ConnectDaemon to check service availability before executing dependent commands, ensuring graceful failure when the daemon is offline.\n- **Input Validation**: Added strict length and character checks for user inputs (e.g., service names, configuration keys) to prevent injection and ensure stability.\n- **Output Formatting**: Added support for JSON and Verbose output modes in commands like Status and Metrics.\n- **Scaffolding**: Provided structured placeholder logic and user-facing workarounds for commands pending full implementation (e.g., Logs, Restart, Metrics).\n\nThis establishes the control flow logic required for the CLI to interact effectively with the application's runtime state.",
			"SHA": "6dad267b44752656629c77165ffe97e4edeaa327"
		}
